Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- extract-exercises.py doesn't detect OpenStax's bold-mathvariant mstyle
  wrapping vector quantities (r, i, j, k, a, v, f, F), so it emitted plain
  \text{r}, \text{i}, etc. instead of \mathbf{...} for the position,
  velocity, acceleration, and force vectors throughout this file (same
  systemic gap already patched for vol3-3-1, vol3-3-2, and vol3-3-3).
  Converted every such occurrence to \mathbf{...}. The scalar radius
  coefficient "r" in item 9's $r\cosh(\omega t)$/$r\sinh(\omega t)$ was
  already typeset as a plain (non-\text) italic variable in the source and
  is left alone, since it is distinct from the bold position vector
  $\mathbf{r}(t)$ in the same expression.
- Item 42's closing sentence "(Recall, $\text{F}=m\cdot \text{a}.)$" trapped
  the sentence-ending period and closing parenthesis inside math mode.
  Moved them outside: "(Recall, $\mathbf{F}=m\cdot \mathbf{a}$.)"
- Several bare prose variables were left as plain text instead of math
  mode: "the parameter t" in the lead-in before item 3, "mass m" and
  "mass M" in items 42 and 44. Wrapped as $t$, $m$, $M$.
- Figure descriptions had bare prose that should be math: "xy plane",
  "y-axis" (twice), and "x axis" in item 1's figure, and "x axis" plus the
  unwrapped "4pi"/"8pi" (with a stray comma) in the cycloid figure.
  Wrapped as $xy$-plane, $y$-axis, $x$-axis, $4\pi$, $8\pi$, and dropped
  the spurious comma before "and".
- The projectile-motion figure description (before item 21) had absorbed
  the following instruction sentence "Answer the following questions."
  inside the \textit{[Figure: ...]} bracket, apparently a converter
  merge of adjacent text nodes. Moved that sentence back out as ordinary
  prose following the figure description.
